3. NEW FUNCTIONS (mesh_analysis.py)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

_generalized_winding_number(point, welded_verts, welded_tris)  [L1557]
    Jacobson et al. 2013 solid-angle sum formula, numpy-vectorised.
    Filters degenerate vectors (|vec| < 1e-15). Returns 0.0 on empty tris.
    O(n) in triangle count.

_same_sign_2d(a, b)  [L1624]
    True when both >0 or both <0. Zero-area (==0) → False (can't be a
    meaningful hole candidate).

_centroid_near_boundary(loop_2d, centroids_2d)  [L1633]
    Checks whether any triangle centroid is within 1% of the loop's
    effective diameter from the nearest loop edge. Uses point-to-segment
    distance (clamped to vertices). Returns True if ANY centroid is
    ambiguous → triggers winding-number fallback.

_compute_interior_probe_3d(loop_pts_2d, loop_pts_3d, normal, origin_3d)
    [L1692]
    Projects the loop's 2D centroid (offset inward by 1% of loop diameter
    toward the farthest vertex) back to 3D using the same u,v basis as
    _project_to_2d (matching ref-selection: abs(n[0]) <= abs(n[1])).

