4. HOLE-CLASSIFICATION CHANGE (decompose_mesh_faces L1962-2016)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

R-5 pre-check inserted before the existing centroid-containment test:

  1. _same_sign_2d(li.signed, outer.signed) → True
     → always merge (same winding direction → cannot be a hole)

  2. Opposite sign:
     a. _loop_contains_centroid → False → hole  (existing behaviour)
     b. _loop_contains_centroid → True  +  _centroid_near_boundary → False
        → merge  (unambiguous centroid test)
     c. _loop_contains_centroid → True  +  _centroid_near_boundary → True
        +  NOT residual_out.get("residual_pairs")
        → _generalized_winding_number
          wn > 0.5 → merge,  wn < 0.5 → hole
     d. residual_out.get("residual_pairs") is truthy  (non-manifold)
        → skip winding number, fall back to centroid result = merge
        (documented as known limitation per plan spec)

The fallback "should_merge = True" in the else branch preserves the
existing behaviour: when the centroid test says "merge" but the winding
number is unavailable (non-manifold), we merge (safe default — avoids
spurious holes).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. DEAD-GUARD BUG (found by orchestrator, fixed)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Original code at L1980:
    if ambiguous and not has_warnings:

Bug: has_warnings is initialized False at L1903 and only set True at L2052,
which runs AFTER the hole-classification loop (L1962-2016). Therefore at
the guard evaluation, has_warnings is ALWAYS False for the current group.
The winding-number guard NEVER blocks — non-manifold meshes get winding
numbers despite the plan's prohibition.

Fix: changed to:
    if ambiguous and not residual_out.get("residual_pairs"):

residual_out is populated by _boundary_loops at L1917 (BEFORE
classification), so residual_pairs reflects the CURRENT group's non-manifold
edge pairs. This is per-group — more precise than the global has_warnings.

NOTE comment updated to reference residual_pairs (R-4) as the per-group
non-manifold signal.

