6. NEW TESTS (tests/test_hole_classification_r5.py)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

test_opposite_signed_area_hole
    Annulus mesh (CCW outer + CW inner). No monkeypatching.
    → 1 face, 1 hole, 4 hole vertices, area=12.0 (16-4).

test_same_signed_merge
    Annulus mesh + monkeypatched _same_sign_2d → True.
    (In a connected 2-manifold mesh, inner loops are always opposite-signed
    after boundary_loops normalisation — so same-sign branch requires
    synthetic triggering.)
    → inner loop merged, no holes, area=16.0.

test_winding_number_fallback_merge
    Annulus + monkeypatched _loop_contains_centroid → True,
    _centroid_near_boundary → True, _generalized_winding_number → 0.95,
    _boundary_loops wrapped to clear residual_pairs.
    → wn > 0.5 → merge, no holes, area=16.0.

test_winding_number_fallback_hole
    Same as above but _generalized_winding_number → 0.12.
    → wn < 0.5 → hole emitted, area=12.0.

test_degenerate_hole_filtered
    4x4 outer, 0.001x0.001 inner (area ~1e-6 << _MIN_FACE_AREA 1e-4).
    → degenerate hole filtered, no holes, area=16.0.

Test idiom: annulus pattern (like _frame_mesh from test_decompose_faces_fix.py).
Winding-number tests wrap _boundary_loops to clear residual_pairs because the
weld's rounded-key grid order reorders vertex indices, creating intermediate
non-manifold edges in _boundary_loops (known T1 weld-grid caveat). Final
decompose output is correct — the residuals are transient.

